                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "38c15264-4dd7-3e8e-aa90-237c6fddc047",
                        "entry_id": "df3c3490-4a1d-3cf3-a6ba-df0664e36988",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An advocate or supporter of eugenics."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2eb134f-9eff-4069-9a25-2ce92d01c0b3",
                                "sense_id": "38c15264-4dd7-3e8e-aa90-237c6fddc047",
                                "text": "And we have enough of this kind of tyranny already ... the world does not want the eugenist to set it straight...."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed4dbb9e-a17d-42c2-927f-4cfc355c0385",
                                "sense_id": "38c15264-4dd7-3e8e-aa90-237c6fddc047",
                                "text": "A man who would throw a bomb at the Russian Czar or at a murderous pogrom-inciting Russian Governor would be considered an assassin, and if caught would be hanged; and in making up the pedigree of such a family, a narrow-minded eugenist would be apt to say that there was criminality in that family."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ab15acd-9bca-4a9e-9f09-e0df3eb054cb",
                                "sense_id": "38c15264-4dd7-3e8e-aa90-237c6fddc047",
                                "text": "When it reported in 1908, it took a strongly hereditarian view of mental deficiency, which was not surprising given that many of its members were paid-up eugenists."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
